  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 131 PM MDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nWednesday...Westerly flow aloft continues and with dry low and mid \nlevels, no precipitation is expected.\n\nThursday...Moist south southwest flow aloft develops in advance of \nthe upper low over Nevada, with deeper moisture and a weak shortwave \ntrough aloft moving across our western counties, producing scattered \nshowers and a few thunderstorms south of a line from Rawlins, to \nWheatland to Cheyenne.\n\nFriday...As the main trough aloft moves across western Wyoming, a \ncold front will lie north to south across our counties, helping to \nproduce scattered showers mainly west of I-25 in the afternoon, and \nspreading eastward in the evening.\n\nSaturday...The primary trough aloft moves overhead early in the day, \nand orographic lift will likely produce scattered showers in the \nafternoon from Douglas to Laramie, and in the evening south of a \nRawlins to Scottsbluff line.\n\nSunday/Monday...Drier conditions return under northwest flow aloft \nand as the low and mid levels dry out somewhat. 700 mb temperatures \nnear 3 Celsius will yield high temperatures in the mid 50s to lower \n60s.",
